{"title":"WBJEE","category":"Engineering","bank":"wbjee","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Amines","count":14,"questions":[{"id":117932,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Amines","exam":"Engineering","examName":"WBJEE","q":"The increasing order of basicity of the following compounds is<br><img style=\"width: 600px\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-self-8e7e11251973a191.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-8e7e11251973a191.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-8e7e11251973a191.png\">\n<img style=\"width: 600px\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fquizrr%2Fquestion-assets%2Fwbjee%2F2026%2Fwatermarked_images%2Fwbjee_2026__q63_d1.png?alt=media\" />","options":["I < III < II","III < I < II","II < I < III","II < III < I"],"answer":0,"solution":"The basicity of amines depends on the availability of the lone pair of electrons on the nitrogen atom for protonation. Greater delocalization of the lone pair decreases its availability, thereby decreasing the basicity of the compound.<br><br>Let us analyze the delocalization of the nitrogen lone pair in each compound:<br><br>1. In compound I, the lone pair on the nitrogen atom is conjugated with the exocyclic double bond and the two double bonds of the ring. Delocalization of this lone pair generates a dipolar resonance structure where the five-membered ring becomes a cyclopentadienyl anion. Since the cyclopentadienyl anion has $6\\pi$ electrons, it is aromatic and highly stable. This strong aromatic stabilization of the ground state makes the lone pair highly delocalized and least available for protonation. Thus, compound I is the least basic.<br><br>2. In compound III, the nitrogen lone pair is in conjugation with the exocyclic double bond, which is further conjugated with the double bond inside the ring. This extended conjugation delocalizes the lone pair over a larger system compared to a simple enamine, reducing its availability for protonation.<br><br>3. In compound II, the nitrogen lone pair is conjugated only with the exocyclic double bond. The double bond inside the ring is isolated and does not participate in conjugation with the nitrogen lone pair. Therefore, the lone pair is the least delocalized among the three compounds and is most available for protonation, making compound II the most basic.<br><br>Comparing the extent of delocalization: I (aromatic stabilization) > III (extended conjugation) > II (simple conjugation).<br><br>Since basicity is inversely proportional to the extent of delocalization of the lone pair, the increasing order of basicity is I < III < II.<br><br>Answer: I < III < II","difficulty":"Hard","source":"WBJEE 2026","_marksId":"6a22caf99b544592bfdee6b8"},{"id":117933,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Amines","exam":"Engineering","examName":"WBJEE","q":"p-nitro-N, N - dimethylaniline cannot be represented by the resonating structures\r\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fwbjee%252F-QrorlbhT45L9COSejzXXiacqECgfQQos4y41RqqyYI.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fwbjee%2F-QrorlbhT45L9COSejzXXiacqECgfQQos4y41RqqyYI.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fwbjee%2F-QrorlbhT45L9COSejzXXiacqECgfQQos4y41RqqyYI.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\">","options":["I and II","II and IV","I and III","III and IV"],"answer":1,"solution":"<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestio